1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,635
The Backpack That Wouldn't Close.

3
00:00:03,635 --> 00:00:07,104
It's Sunday evening, and my backpack refuses to close.

4
00:00:07,104 --> 00:00:10,792
I pull the zipper, push on the top, and try asking nicely.

5
00:00:10,792 --> 00:00:12,323
Nothing works.

6
00:00:12,323 --> 00:00:14,937
Dad walks past my door and stops.

7
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,982
Do you need all of that?

8
00:00:17,212 --> 00:00:18,414
Probably.

9
00:00:18,414 --> 00:00:19,612
Maybe.

10
00:00:19,612 --> 00:00:21,477
I'm prepared for everything.

11
00:00:21,748 --> 00:00:23,554
Let's take everything out.

12
00:00:23,554 --> 00:00:26,398
Then we can see what everything actually means.

13
00:00:26,668 --> 00:00:28,537
We put my things on the bed.

14
00:00:28,537 --> 00:00:35,599
Three notebooks, two library books, a pencil case, a sweater, an old art project, and a rock that looks a little like a potato.

15
00:00:35,884 --> 00:00:38,105
Is the rock part of your homework?

16
00:00:38,332 --> 00:00:39,451
No.

17
00:00:39,451 --> 00:00:41,232
I found it last week.

18
00:00:41,232 --> 00:00:43,211
It has a nice personality.

19
00:00:43,492 --> 00:00:45,757
Then it can keep your desk company.

20
00:00:45,757 --> 00:00:47,538
That can stay at home.

21
00:00:47,812 --> 00:00:49,702
I check tomorrow's schedule.

22
00:00:49,702 --> 00:00:53,597
I only need two notebooks, and the art project was finished days ago.

23
00:00:53,597 --> 00:00:56,972
One library book is due tomorrow, so that goes back in.

24
00:00:57,244 --> 00:00:59,204
Can I have the potato rock?

25
00:00:59,428 --> 00:01:01,474
You may visit it on my desk.

26
00:01:01,474 --> 00:01:03,349
It's not ready to move out.

27
00:01:03,349 --> 00:01:07,307
I put the heavier books close to the back and the smaller things in the front pocket.

28
00:01:07,307 --> 00:01:09,901
The zipper finally closes without a fight.

29
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:11,911
How does it feel now?

30
00:01:12,148 --> 00:01:13,444
Much better.

31
00:01:13,444 --> 00:01:16,704
I lift the backpack with one hand, then try it on.

32
00:01:16,704 --> 00:01:19,079
Ben watches carefully from the doorway.

33
00:01:19,348 --> 00:01:21,277
Your bag looks happier.

34
00:01:21,508 --> 00:01:23,273
So do my shoulders.

35
00:01:23,273 --> 00:01:26,689
The rock remains on my desk, looking quietly supportive.

36
00:01:26,689 --> 00:01:30,470
Tomorrow, I will be prepared for school, which is probably enough.
